        "title": "07 - International Law",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\n┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│                    INTERNATIONAL LAW FRAMEWORK                           │\n├──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│                                                                          │\n│  PUBLIC INTERNATIONAL LAW        PRIVATE INTERNATIONAL LAW              │\n│  (between states/nations)        (cross-border private transactions)    │\n│  ──────────────────────          ──────────────────────────────          │\n│  Treaties + Conventions          Choice of law                          │\n│  Customary int'l law             Choice of forum                        │\n│  UN Charter / ICJ                Enforcement of foreign judgments       │\n│  WTO dispute settlement          International arbitration              │\n│  Diplomatic immunity             Investment arbitration (BITs)          │\n│  Sovereign immunity                                                      │\n│                                                                          │\n├──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│                                                                          │\n│  SOURCES OF INT'L LAW (ICJ Statute Art. 38):                             │\n│  (1) International conventions/treaties (express consent)                │\n│  (2) International custom (general state practice + opinio juris)        │\n│  (3) General principles recognized by civilized nations                  │\n│  (4) Judicial decisions + scholarly writings (subsidiary sources)        │\n│                                                                          │\n└──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n```"
    }
